{"id":"vie-t0-0001","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.hello","domain":1,"text_native":"Chào.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Hello.","source_caption":"Hello.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The default greeting anywhere. Works with every age and every status.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0002","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.morning","domain":1,"text_native":"sáng","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Good morning.","source_caption":"morning","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Used until roughly midday. Getting the time of day wrong is noticed; not saying it is only noticed by someone expecting it.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0003","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.afternoon","domain":1,"text_native":"chiều","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Good afternoon.","source_caption":"afternoon","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The middle of the day. In several languages this is the same word as the evening greeting, and using it late is not an error.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0004","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.evening","domain":1,"text_native":"Good evening.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Good evening.","source_caption":"Good evening.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"From late afternoon. Often interchangeable with the afternoon greeting.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0005","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.what-is-your-name","domain":1,"text_native":"Ông tên là gì?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"What is your name?","source_caption":"What is your name?)","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"You get asked this before you get to ask it. Recognising the question is the difference between answering and freezing.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0006","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"greeting.learning","domain":1,"text_native":"Tôi đang học.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am learning your language.","source_caption":"I am learning.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Sets the whole interaction. Said once, early, it buys patience you would otherwise have to spend on being incomprehensible — and it is the difference between being ignored and being helped.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":"In several of these languages there is a separate, more formal phrase for a learner talking to an elder or an official. The neutral one can read as flippancy in a formal setting.","source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba vie-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"11326303","author":"TATAR1"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0007","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.please","domain":1,"text_native":"Làm ơn.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Please.","source_caption":"Please.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Not a filler in English, and a grammatical particle in some of these languages — one word that changes a sentence from an order to a request.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0008","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.thank-you","domain":1,"text_native":"Cảm ơn.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Thank you.","source_caption":"Thank you.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The single most useful word in any of these languages. Saying it costs nothing and changes how everything after it is received.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0009","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.youre-welcome","domain":1,"text_native":"Không sao đâu.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"You are welcome.","source_caption":"You're welcome.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"You will be handed it constantly, and there is no way to avoid replying. In a few languages the reply is the same word as 'yes'.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0010","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.excuse-me","domain":1,"text_native":"Excuse me.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Excuse me.","source_caption":"Excuse me. (begging pardon)","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Two different things in one phrase: getting someone's attention, and getting past them. Guessing wrong is jarring — one version walks through a conversation.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0011","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"courtesy.sorry","domain":1,"text_native":"Xin lỗi.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I am sorry.","source_caption":"I'm sorry.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"Apologising for a small fault — bumping someone, being late, not understanding. The form you use signals how much of a fault you think it was.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0012","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"repair.dont-understand","domain":12,"text_native":"Tôi không hiểu.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I do not understand.","source_caption":"I don't understand.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The one phrase that keeps a conversation alive. Without it people stop trying, and with it they often rephrase in simpler words.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0013","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"repair.help-me","domain":12,"text_native":"Hãy giúp tôi.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Can you help me, please?","source_caption":"Help me.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The opener for every request that follows. Standing in front of someone not being asked anything is how people get ignored.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba vie-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"8948855","author":"Zifre"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0014","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"repair.dont-know","domain":12,"text_native":"Tôi không biết.","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"I do not know.","source_caption":"I have no idea.","register":"neutral","direction":"say","why":"The honest answer, and in some cultures the only acceptable one — guessing when you don't know reads as deceit rather than as effort.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba vie-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"5670","author":"CK"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0015","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"bridge.understand","domain":12,"text_native":"Bạn hiểu không?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do you understand?","source_caption":"Do you understand?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"You get asked it after anything you say, and the honest answer is the only useful one.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"attested","id":"Tatoeba vie-en sentence pairs (CC BY 2.0 FR)","url":"https://tatoeba.org/en/downloads","licence":"CC BY 2.0 FR, some CC0","external_id":"13136034","author":"Ramses"},"failure_flags":[]}
{"id":"vie-t0-0016","lang":"vie","tier":0,"slot":"bridge.speak-english","domain":12,"text_native":"Biết nói tiếng Anh không?","text_romanized":null,"text_english":"Do you speak English?","source_caption":"Do you speak English?","register":"neutral","direction":"understand","why":"Asked of you constantly, and the question that decides whether anything after it can happen. There is a polite version and a blunt version and the gap between them is wide.","exchange_id":null,"exchange_turn":null,"caution":null,"source":{"class":"curated","id":"Wikivoyage: Vietnamese phrasebook","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/Vietnamese_phrasebook","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0","external_id":null,"author":null},"failure_flags":[]}
